# Airflow

DAGs: `orchestration/airflow/dags/`. Plugins: `orchestration/airflow/plugins/`.

## Current DAGs

| DAG | Owns |
|---|---|
| `warehouse_daily_batch_pipeline` | POS Parquet, `WAREHOUSE_LIVE_MODELS`, **`marts.finance`**, ANALYZE |
| `marketing_hourly_customer_360_pipeline` | EMR Spark identity step (GraphFrames, ADR-010) → WAP clone → `MARKETING_LIVE_MODELS` + **`marts.marketing`** (sessions, RFM, C360) |
| `streaming_manual_flink_jobs` | EMR Flink submit via `streaming/bin/submit_flink_job.sh` (YARN duplicate guard, checkpoint restore) |
| `catalog_bihourly_product_scd2_refresh` | `CATALOG_LIVE_MODELS` + `dim_product` SCD2 |
| `quality_hourly_ge_checkpoint` | Hourly GE `silver_events_daily` (Silver events only) + metadata freshness SLA |
| `lakehouse_daily_iceberg_maintenance` | Spark Iceberg compaction / snapshot expiry (`spark/maintenance/`) |

Staging/intermediate models build live (not WAP). Each has exactly one building
DAG, listed in `plugins/dbt_selectors.py`; never select `staging` or
`intermediate` wholesale.

Do not dual-build `marts.marketing` on the daily warehouse DAG.

## Write-Audit-Publish (ADR-009)

Gold marts are clone → write → audit → publish. A failing audit leaves live intact.

- Each owning DAG clones its live tables into `*_pending`, runs dbt with
  `wap_phase=pending`, audits with `dbt test` + `pending_tables` (reconcile),
  then publishes. GE does not audit Gold.
- Table list lives in `plugins/wap_publish.py` (`WAP_TABLES` + disjoint per-DAG
  subsets). `dim_product` is catalog-only. `dim_date`/`dim_store` excluded.
- No-MWAA laptop runs: `python plugins/wap_publish.py <clone|publish>
  <finance|marketing|catalog>` — `WAP_SCOPES` reuses the same ownership sets;
  connects via `RS_*` env vars, never hardcoded credentials.
## Conventions

- Filename/DAG ID: `{domain}_{frequency}_{description}`.
- `doc_md`, `catchup=False`, retries, `execution_timeout`, and
  `on_failure_callback: notify_task_failure` (SNS via the `alert_topic_arn`
  Variable). MWAA has no SMTP: never use `email_on_failure`. CI loads the
  DagBag (`tests/integration/verify_dagbag.py`) and fails a task without both.
- Infra endpoints via Airflow Variables — no hardcoded ARNs/passwords/endpoints.
- Never template a secret into a command: Jinja renders `{{ var.value.* }}` into
  the stored command, the Rendered Template tab, and task logs. dbt tasks use
  `dbt_task_bash` and GE tasks `ge_bash_with_metadata`, which export
  `RS_SECRET_ARN` and fetch the password in the task shell; Python tasks call
  `metadata_airflow.redshift_password()`. Enforced by `tests/unit/test_dag_contract.py`.
- dbt runs from `$DBT_BIN`, a virtualenv the MWAA startup script builds from
  `infra/terraform/modules/mwaa/dbt-requirements.txt`; dbt cannot share the
  Airflow 2.8.1 constraints. `dbt_task_bash` syncs a private project copy per
  task because consecutive tasks may run on different workers.
- MWAA `requirements.txt` starts with the Airflow constraints line; do not pin
  packages the constraints file already pins.
- Prefer task factories (`_dbt_step`, `_flink_step`).
- Idempotency: no duplicate Flink submits; partition-safe POS; dbt `delete+insert` uniqueness.
